{% extends "base.html.j2" %}

{% from "_formhelpers.html.j2" import render_field %}
{% from "_projecthelpers.html.j2" import render_datasets, navbar, cancel %}

{% block content %}

{% include '_header.html.j2' %}

<div class="mui-panel">
  {{ navbar(project, "Create session") }}
  <div class="mui-panel">
    <h1>Create session in project "{{ project['name'] }}"</h1>

    {% include '_flash.html.j2' %}
    <p>Sessions are folders directly inside a project folder that contain a <code>raw</code> subfolder.
    They offer two features that are important for managing microscopy data:
    <ul>
      <li>Their ingest shares can be mapped on instrument computers using modama-agent
      to facilitate saving data with the correct ownership and access rights for a project.</li>
      <li>They can be sealed, which means that the <code>raw</code> subfolder and its contents are
      immutable: nobody can change, rename or delete them. It is strongly recommended to place microscopy data and important notes in the
      <code>raw</code> subfolder and seal sessions in a timely manner to prevent data loss through
      user error or malicious software.</li>
    </ul>
    Project members are free to create files and folders within a session as they see fit.
    The session folder itself and any content except the <code>raw</code> subfolder remain writable after sealing.
    </p>
    <p>
    Administrators can seal and unseal any files and folders in the data management system on request.
    </p>
    <form
        method=post
        action="{{ url_for("create_dataset", name=project.name) }}"
        class="mui-form"
    >
      {{ form.csrf_token }}
      <dl>
        {{ render_field(form.name) }}
      </dl>
      <p>
        <input type="submit" class="mui-btn mui-btn--raised mui-btn--primary" value="Create session">
        {{ cancel(project) }}
      </p>
    </form>
  </div>
  <div class="mui-panel">
    <h2>Current sessions</h2>

    {{ render_datasets(project, datasets, current_user)}}
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock content %}